Z||000005||fieroshop||04-14-2000||12:32 AM||||Well it seem that you are going for price and not longevity of a clutc. I offer double you last clutch miles warranty. Which means that if you had 25,000 miles on your previous clutch I will give you 50,000 mile warranty. You probably ask catch, no catch just a simple item. You must resurface your flywheel or install anew one. My clutch is 100% kevlar and not a composit like most clutches. Before you buy check out if Chris West is a kevlar or a composit or stock. You get what you pay for.||||reg||6
Z||000006||1FST2M6||04-14-2000||08:58 AM||||the shop i deal with doesn't like Centerforce.. cause mine failed... along with about 5 others... (S/C Civic, S/C GS-R, 94 Toyota truck, 86 SE Fiero{mine} and others) I'm sure they are GREAT for a car with a decent space for their weights to work right eg. Moostang, camaro etc. but they aren't that great, from my experiance.. I'd go with Chris Wests kit if your just looking for an upgrade... I have more of a full race set up now, and we have been able to adapt my clutch pack and a friends to make a drivable stop light monster.    <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>   or the Fieroshop unit... he's right.. you do get what you pay for! I'm sorry fieroshop i'm not familiar with your stuff... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieroshop||04-14-2000||10:48 AM||||I also don't know of Chris West clutch. I will say that if he is using the same clutch as FOCOA then I will say my clutch is far superior. So far we have outperformed these clutches, ram, centerforce, focoa not to metion all aftermarket stock clutches. If any of you have heard or talked with Michael Smith he can tell you some experiences hes has with all these clutches. I know that when he is ready for another clutch he will be installing my clutch in his 225 hp dual overhead cam 3.4 that he has installed in his 66 GT.<BR>Check out my clutch at <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 04-14-2000).]||||reg||1
